# The Fingerprint HAL — An Agnostic, Device-Internal Transactional Contract [SPEC:CXC-FPHALC]

> One contract, N implementations. `R503HAL` speaks to real hardware; `MockFingerprintHAL` speaks to
> an in-memory dict. Neither is privileged as an *architecture* — both are peer implementations of one
> interface — but the mock IS the canonical *reference*: where the two disagree on a parity assertion,
> the mock is the expected value and `R503HAL` is the actual, because the mock's behaviour is fully
> specified by this document and the part's is inferred from a datasheet with self-contradictions
> across four revisions.
>
> This contract runs entirely on the device. Its only caller is the device's own firmware; nothing
> above ComposeBus ever imports a HAL module or calls a HAL method. The bus messages
> ([SPEC:CXC-FPBUSC]) are what the firmware builds on top of this contract, not a reflection of it.

---

## 1. Two faces, one contract

### [CXC-FPHALC-TWO-FACES] The runtime face is a plain call; only enrollment pays a ceremony

- constraint: `capabilities()` and `match()` are plain, value-returning calls — one call, one value, no state to persist and nothing to resume. `begin_enroll()` returns a separately-typed session whose only advancing method, `step()`, advances by at most one interaction and returns immediately, because enrollment is the one operation with a human in the middle of it and cannot block a tick loop.
- rationale: a runtime-only consumer never constructs a session and never names an enrollment phase. The ceremony's state lives in the session object, never in the HAL.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FPHALC]

---

## 2. The contract

### [CXC-FPHALC-PROTOCOL-SURFACE] Nine operations, fully typed

```python
class FingerprintHAL(Protocol):
    """One contract, N implementations. Every method may fail with
    FingerprintHALError, carrying one of the six closed axes of
    FailureAxis."""

    def capabilities(self) -> Capabilities: ...
    """MANDATORY. Total, side-effect-free, stable for the life of the object."""

    def match(self) -> MatchResult: ...
    """Capture once, search the resident set. Returns an outcome, and a
    slot plus a device-internal score IFF matched. No verdict of any kind —
    this HAL has no concept of person, role or capability."""

    def begin_enroll(self, ordinal: Ordinal) -> EnrollmentSession: ...
    """Returns immediately with a session that has captured nothing.
    No slot argument: slot is a device-internal capture-buffer detail,
    never externally addressed."""

    def write_template(self, template: TemplateBytes) -> Slot: ...
    """Write one opaque template into the next available internal slot
    and return which slot it landed in, for the caller's own bookkeeping.
    The push firmware calls this once per entry while loading a set."""

    def read_template(self, slot: Slot) -> TemplateBytes: ...
    """CAPABILITY-GATED on supports_readback. Its purpose is to extract a
    freshly captured template so the enrollment station's application
    layer can upload it to fingerprint_storage — not an identity audit."""

    def delete_slot(self, slot: Slot) -> None: ...
    """IDEMPOTENT: deleting an unoccupied slot succeeds."""

    def empty(self) -> None: ...
    """Destroy every resident template. IDEMPOTENT. Does not touch the
    stamp; the caller clears the stamp separately so a device interrupted
    between the two never testifies to a roster it does not hold."""

    def write_template_set_uuid(self, uuid: str | None) -> None: ...
    """Write the stamp durably. None clears it. TESTIMONY, not proof: the
    device's own claim about which set it holds."""

    def read_template_set_uuid(self) -> str | None: ...
    """None means no set has EVER been loaded, distinct from a value
    nobody wrote over."""

    def command_feedback(
        self,
        state: FeedbackState,
        progress: EnrollProgress | None = None,
    ) -> None: ...
    """The ONLY method that writes feedback, and it takes the state as an
    argument. Nothing else on this contract, and nothing on
    EnrollmentSession, may write feedback — the device is the one writer,
    always, including mid-enrollment."""
```

- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FPHALC]
- see-also: [CXC-FPHALC-CAPABILITIES-SCHEMA], [CXC-FPHALC-FAILURE-AXES], [CXC-FPHALC-FEEDBACK-INVARIANT]

### [CXC-FPHALC-STAMP-FORMAT] The stamp is one UUID, and nothing on this contract hashes anything

- constraint: `write_template_set_uuid` / `read_template_set_uuid` carry a single opaque string — the pushed set's `template_set_uuid` — and nothing else. No hash of any kind is computed, stored, or compared anywhere in this contract.
- rationale: identity is the UUID; completeness of a load is that every entry the wire contract promised was written successfully. A low-end MCU cannot hash up to twenty templates in a time budget worth defending, and nothing downstream of this contract needs it to.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FPHALC]

### [CXC-FPHALC-ENROLLMENT-SESSION-SURFACE] The enrollment session steps, reports, and holds no path to feedback

```python
class EnrollmentSession(Protocol):
    """NO FEEDBACK METHOD, by construction."""

    ordinal: Ordinal

    def step(self) -> EnrollStep: ...
    """Advance by at most one interaction and return immediately."""

    def cancel(self) -> None: ...
    """Abandon. IDEMPOTENT."""


class EnrollPhase(Enum):
    AWAITING_FINGER = "awaiting_finger"
    CAPTURE_ACCEPTED = "capture_accepted"
    CAPTURE_RETRY = "capture_retry"
    MERGING = "merging"
    STORED = "stored"          # TERMINAL, success
    CANCELLED = "cancelled"    # TERMINAL
    FAILED = "failed"          # TERMINAL, carries a FingerprintHALFailure


@dataclass(frozen=True)
class EnrollProgress:
    ordinal: Ordinal
    capture_n: int
    capture_of: int   # == capabilities().captures_per_template
```

- constraint: the session type has no feedback method and no reference to one. The invariant that the HAL never drives feedback is therefore a compile-time property of this type, not a code-review item.
- status: draft
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-FPHALC]
- see-also: [CXC-FPHALC-FEEDBACK-INVARIANT]

